{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/792029-kinships-of-those-who-are-no-more","id":792029,"title":"Kinships of Those who are No More","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-24T00:14:56-08:00","id":792029,"title":"Kinships of Those who are No More","content":"The Children of the Dark Mother have all many of relations with the paranormal critters of the Chronicles WoD. This can have a big impact upon them. Creating Nightmares, adding Havens/Loci/Hallows/Trod/Avernian Gates/Tombs etc to their Lairs as befits their allegiances.<br /> <br /> So how does it effect the Begotten when one such ally passes beyond the veil? For the sake of clarity, let me state this plainly; we're talking Final Death, Leaves No Ghost Behind, No Ritual For A New Body kind of no more appearances. And in order to explore this fully, let us assume it was an exceedingly close relationship; exchanging rings &amp; vows, soul-sharing sacred spaces sort of relationship.<br /> <br /> I am asking what do you think would be the 'aspect/flavour' changes to the mystical component of the Beast, in the wake of such a loss.<br /> <br /> Naturally this will vary drastically between individuals, and I can already foresee the whole 'not necessary' comments. That is not what I am asking for; I want to hear people's ideas on the matter, how they think it can improve a story. If you have the Loci your werewolf lover preposed at as a Lair Chamber, does that Chamber change in 'mood' after said fianc\u00e9 has met their end at the hands of host/pure/idigam/claimed/hunters/etc? Does the Nightmare born from your Mastigos brother's psychic interrogation techniques taste different to you after the Seers have stripped him of his soul and slit his throat?<br /> <br /> I also ask that you try to refrain from to general an answer; use the splats &amp; their factions to help but don't say 'Vampires' or 'Changelings'; say 'a fledging Deva Sanctified' or 'an Autumn Leechfinger Ogre'. Details are what makes characters and the relationships between them special. Heck, if you want, use concepts or characters that you've used in the past. Have fun with it, at least as much as you can given it is a fundamentally tragic query.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T03:01:31-08:00","id":792071,"title":"","content":"I think that it would probably change. It would likely become tainted with a combination of the Beast's grief and mourning and the Horror's fury at the ones who took them. Maybe it becomes crueller to those of the same alliances (e.g. other Seers of the Throne etc).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T21:49:51-08:00","id":792552,"title":"","content":"Tangentially related line of inquiry:<br /> <br /> Is Kinship transitive in any fashion? For instance, does developing Kinship with a Claimed who dies leave you with Kinship with the newly-discarnate spirit? Do your Kindred family's childer count as kin by default? Does having Kinship with a geist give you Kinship with a Sin-Eater that it makes a Bargain with? And so on down the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T09:29:27-08:00","id":792757,"title":"","content":"Family Ties would end, but the Nightmares and added Chambers would remain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T14:30:46-08:00","id":792834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/792029-kinships-of-those-who-are-no-more?p=792757#post792757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Family Ties would end, but the Nightmares and added Chambers would remain.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd even take it that the Flavour of the Nightmares remain too, The things people do that frighten aren't suddenly going to change because the person you learned it from isn't around any more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}